---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Terms of Service — Try Convi"
  description="The terms that govern your use of Try Convi."
>
  <article class="legal">
    <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
    <p class="updated">Last updated: 16 July 2026</p>

    <p>
      These terms govern your use of Try Convi ("the service"), available at
      <a href="https://tryconvi.com">tryconvi.com</a>. By using the service you
      agree to these terms.
    </p>

    <h2>What Try Convi is</h2>
    <p>
      Try Convi is a language-learning tool with browsable conversation
      scenarios and a paid Practice mode. It's an educational aid, not a
      guarantee of fluency, and the colloquial phrases and slang it teaches are
      provided for learning and entertainment.
    </p>

    <h2>Accounts and access</h2>
    <p>
      Browsing scenarios is free. Practice mode is unlocked with a one-time
      purchase tied to the email you buy with. Your access is for your personal,
      non-commercial use. Please don't share, resell, or redistribute paid
      content.
    </p>

    <h2>Purchases and refunds</h2>
    <p>
      Payments are processed by Gumroad as the merchant of record, subject to
      their terms. Applicable taxes (such as VAT) may be added at checkout.
      Refund requests are handled according to our refund policy and Gumroad's
      procedures — contact us and we'll help.
    </p>

    <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
    <p>
      Don't misuse the service: no attempting to break, overload, scrape at
      scale, or gain unauthorized access to our systems, and no using the
      content unlawfully.
    </p>

    <h2>Intellectual property</h2>
    <p>
      The Try Convi name, content, and design are owned by us. Your purchase
      grants you a personal license to use the content, not ownership of it.
    </p>

    <h2>Disclaimer</h2>
    <p>
      The service is provided "as is" without warranties of any kind. Language
      is living and regional — we aim for accuracy but can't guarantee every
      phrase fits every situation. Use good judgement, especially with slang.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      We may update these terms as the service evolves. Continued use after
      changes means you accept the updated terms.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about these terms? Email
      <a href="mailto:hello@tryconvi.com">hello@tryconvi.com</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</Layout>

<style>
  .legal {
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .legal h1 {
    margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
  }

  .legal .updated {
    color: var(--color-ink-soft);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  .legal h2 {
    margin-top: 2rem;
    font-size: 1.25rem;
  }

  .legal a {
    color: var(--color-primary);
  }
</style>
